  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increased capacity of Member States to ratify international labour standards</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The following are the major global deliverables and activities of the ILO in this policy area.
(1) facilitate the engagement of constituents in the adoption and implementation of the recommendations of the SRM TWG at all levels, as approved by the Governing Body;
(2) targeted promotional activities to support Member States in considering steps to ratify and apply in national law and practice the international labour standards relevant to decent work in supply chains, with special attention to the instruments giving expression to all five fundamental principles and rights at work, and the governance Conventions
(3) in collaboration with the Turin Centre, expanded opportunities for the use of information technology and distance learning in response to the constituents&#x2019; needs, ensuring access to practical and user-friendly information and capacity-building that is of relevance for ratification, reporting and effective application.
(4)   promotion of the international labour standards that are particularly relevant to a renewed social contract and the thematic priorities of the Coalition, including the Social Security (Minimum Standards) Convention, 1952 (No. 102).</narrative>
  </description>
